    "tx_nd_dwi_deferred-proof-of-delivery-to-prosecutor-3": "Used only where local practice requires the filer to deliver a copy to the prosecuting attorney. Gov't Code § 411.0745(e) makes the COURT responsible for notifying the state and the filer should not be charged for that notice; OCA instructions nonetheless direct the petitioner to show proof that the district attorney received a copy. Ask the clerk which applies in that county.",
